<%- include('../partials/header', { title: 'System Settings — Inicio Diary', user }) %>

<%#
  Platform-wide operational settings. Superadmin-only, and deliberately not on
  a study's own Settings page: the scheduler is one Node process serving every
  study, so how often it checks for anything due is necessarily a platform
  choice, not a per-study one. A study's own reminder TIMES stay where they
  already were, in Study Settings -- this is the different, coarser thing
  underneath them.
%>
<div class="max-w-xl">
  <div class="mb-6">
    <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-brand-500 uppercase tracking-wide mb-0.5">Platform</div>
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">System Settings</h1>
    <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm mt-1">Operational settings for the whole platform, not any one study.</p>
  </div>

  <% if (saved) { %>
    <div class="mb-5 rounded-xl border border-verified/30 bg-verified-soft px-4 py-3 text-sm text-verified">
      Saved. The scheduler will pick this up on its next cycle &mdash; no restart needed.
    </div>
  <% } %>

  <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/70 shadow-card p-6">
    <div class="font-semibold text-slate-800 mb-1">Background check interval</div>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
      How often the platform checks whether any reminder or end-of-diary validation is due, across every
      study. This used to be fixed by an Azure environment variable that only someone with infrastructure
      access could change &mdash; it's a setting now, not a deployment detail.
    </p>

    <form method="POST" action="/admin/system-settings" class="flex items-end gap-3">
      <div>
        <label class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-wide mb-1.5">Minutes between checks</label>
        <input type="number" name="scheduler_interval_minutes" value="<%= currentMinutes %>"
               min="<%= minMinutes %>" max="<%= maxMinutes %>" required
               class="w-32 rounded-xl border border-slate-300 px-3.5 py-2.5 text-base focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-brand-400" />
      </div>
      <button class="bg-brand-700 text-white rounded-xl px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold hover:bg-brand-600 transition">Save</button>
    </form>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-3">Allowed range: <%= minMinutes %>\u2013<%= maxMinutes %> minutes.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-5 leading-relaxed">
    This does not change any study's own reminder times (first/second reminder, quiet hours) &mdash; those
    stay in each study's own Settings &amp; Thresholds. This is how often the platform wakes up to check
    whether any of those times, across every study, have now arrived.
  </p>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
